# Rebased Character Identity SQLite Engine & Tournament Auto-Suggest — Implementation Plan

## Context
The Manager requested moving Character Identity from flat JSON files (`Hazard_Trigger_Data/Identity/Characters/TT01/A01.json`) into an authoritative relational SQLite database following the **Entropy Rose** architectural style. In tournaments, rather than typing arbitrary names or creating ad-hoc entries, the Manager wants to specify competitors solely by their **Character ID** via an **auto-suggest selector** (with options strictly constrained to existing character IDs in the SQLite database, with "no create new").

---

## 1. Schema & Hex ID Design (Rose Relational Pattern)

### Hex ID Prefix Standards (`<System "1"><3-Hex-Type><12-Hex-Timestamp>`)
- `1001` — Tournaments
- `1002` — Tournament Matches / Bracket Slots
- `1003` — Tournament Participants / Seeds
- **`1004`** — Characters (Identity Entities)
- **`1005`** — Character Variants / Outfits

### Relational Schema Definition (`backend/character_db.py`)

```sql
-- Table: characters (1004...)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS characters (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                 -- 1004... 16-character monotonic hex ID
    char_code TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,      -- Character Code e.g. 'A01', 'B28', 'B53', 'C14'
    canonical_name TEXT NOT NULL,        -- Primary Name e.g. 'Amelia Watson'
    series TEXT,                         -- World / Series / Franchise e.g. 'Hololive', 'Azur Lane'
    associate_json TEXT,                 -- Association array e.g. '["HoloMyth"]'
    names_json TEXT,                     -- { names: [...], nicknames: [...], aliases: [...] }
    hazard_score REAL DEFAULT 0.0,       -- Plain decimal odometer <a.b> (e.g. 3.0)
    hazard_class TEXT,                   -- Class I..V classification badge
    base_prompt TEXT,                    -- _prpt_ visual token string
    outfit TEXT,                         -- Default outfit token string
    avatar_url TEXT,                     -- Image/Avatar URL or relative path
    taxonomy_json TEXT,                  -- { archetype: [], personalityTropes: [], addressment: [] }
    dna_phase1_json TEXT,                -- Physical traits: hair, eyes, physique
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_characters_char_code ON characters(char_code);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_characters_name ON characters(canonical_name);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_characters_series ON characters(series);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_characters_hazard ON characters(hazard_score);

-- Table: character_variants (1005...)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS character_variants (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                 -- 1005... 16-character monotonic hex ID
    character_id TEXT NOT NULL,          -- Foreign key to characters(id)
    variant_key TEXT NOT NULL,           -- e.g. 'default', 'ego_01', 'skin_01'
    variant_name TEXT NOT NULL,          -- e.g. 'The Casual Ame'
    prompt TEXT,                         -- Variant prompt tokens
    outfit TEXT,                         -- Variant outfit tokens
    is_default INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (character_id) REFERENCES characters(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    UNIQUE(character_id, variant_key)
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_cv_char ON character_variants(character_id);
```

